hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"5611","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: I am Abdullah bin Wahb, he said: Al-Dahhak bin Uthman narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Al-Nadr, on the authority of Busr bin Saeed, on the authority of Zayd bin Khaled Al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about the snapshot. He said: Define it for a year. If not “You know, so know its safekeeping and its stewards, then all of it. When its owner comes, give it to him.” On the authority of Harun bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abi Fadiq, and Abi Bakr Al-Hanafi, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Uthman, with it"
"5612","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim told me, he said: Asad bin Musa told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, And Rabi’ah, on the authority of Yazid, the client of the Prophet, on the authority of Zaid bin Khaled, that a man asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “about stray camels.” He asked him about the lot, and he said: Know its properties, its agents, and their number. Then he identified it for a year. If its owner comes and knows its properties, And its number and agent, so give it to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5613","Ishaq bin Ismail told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Rabi’ah, on the authority of Yazid, the client of the Prophet, on the authority of Zayd bin Khalid Al-Juhani said that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He was asked about the shoot, and he said: Know its properties and its properties, and he recognized it.” Sunnah, if it is recognized, otherwise mix it with your money.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5614","Muhammad bin Salamah informed us, saying: I am Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Rabi’ah, on the authority of Yazid, the client of al-Manba’th, on the authority of Zaid Ibn Khalid, he said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him about the shoot, and he said: Know its strength and its protection. Then let it be known for a year, and if its owner comes along, otherwise it is up to you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5615","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Rabi’ah, on the authority of Yazid, the client of the Prophet, on the authority of Zaid bin Khaled Al-Juhani, that A man asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “about the shoot, and he said: Find out about it for a year, then find out its measure, and its purity, then spend, If its owner comes, give it back to him.” Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: This hadith was narrated on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Rabia, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, on the authority of a man, mursal with another wording. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5616","5658 Yazid bin Muhammad bin Abdul Samad told us, he said: Ali bin Ayyash told us, he said: Al-Layth told me, he said: He who was satisfied told me, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Abi Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, the client of al-Manbu’th, on the authority of a man among the companions of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked “about the stray animal,” and he said: “Know its safeties and its protection.” Then he introduced it to the door for three days. The mosque, if its owner comes, give it to him, and if he does not come, let him know it for a year, then if its owner comes, otherwise your business with it.” Abu Abdul Rahman told us: This hadith was narrated by Abbad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Zaid. Bin Khalid (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5617","Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Ibrahim bin Tahman told me, on the authority of Abbad, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Yazid, on the authority of his father Yazid, the client of Al-Manba’th, on the authority of Zayd Ibn Khalid Al-Juhani, that he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked He said “about the stray sheep,” and he was asked about the shoot. He said: “You know it is one year old. If its owner comes, you give it to him. Otherwise, you know its age.” Or he said: Its chastity and then it is your money, so if its owner comes, you will give it to him."
"5618","Abu Ubaidah bin Abi Al-Safar told us, he said: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Kathir, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Amr and Asim My two sons, Sufyan bin Abdullah, on the authority of their father, that: “He picked up a blemish, and Omar met it, and he said to me: Show it to me, and when he was with... Qarn al-‘Awl, I met him with it, and said: I recognized it, but you did not acknowledge it. He said: It is yours. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us. With that, I said: I have no need for it, so he ordered that it be thrown into the treasury.”"
"5619","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Jesus, meaning Ibn Yunus. He said: Al-Walid bin Kathir told us, he said: Jesus, and Al-Walid was trustworthy in hadith. On the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Asim, and Amr bin Sufyan bin Abdullah, “Sufyan bin Abdullah” found a defect, so he brought it Omar Ibn Al-Khattab said: Know it for a year, and if it is known then with that, otherwise it is yours. It was not known, so I found it the following year from So I mentioned it to him, and he said: It is yours. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us to do so. He said: I have no need of it, so he took it. Omar, and put it in the treasury.”"
"5620","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ told us, he said: Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abdul Aziz, who is the son of Abi Salamah al-Majishun, told us, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Al-Fadl, on the authority of Salamah Ibn Kuhail, he said: Suwayd Ibn Ghafla, Zayd Ibn Suhan, and a third were with them on a journey, and he found one of them A whip, so he took it, and his two companions said to him: Throw it away. He said: Enjoy it. If its owner comes, I will give it to him. It is better than Leave it to be eaten by wild beasts. He met Ubayy ibn Ka’b and mentioned that to him. Ubayy ibn Ka’b said: “I found one hundred dinars in the time of the Messenger of God.” God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I brought her to him, and he said: He recognized her for a year. I recognized her, but she was not recognized. So I returned, and he said: He recognized her for a year. He recognized it generally twice or three times, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Know its number, its container, and its agent. And mix it for your owner, and if its owner comes, give it to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5621","Muhammad ibn Qudamah told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Suwayd ibn Ghafla, he said: We were pilgrims, and I found a whip So I took it, and I met Ubayy bin Ka’b, and I mentioned that to him, and he said: You have done well. Then he said to me: “I picked up a bundle containing a hundred dinars, so I came.” The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I mentioned that to him, and he said: He knew her for a year, so I knew her for a year, so I said: I knew her for a year, so he said He introduced her another year, so I introduced her another year, then I came to him, and I said: I knew her one year, and he said: He introduced her another year, then I came to him. So I said: I knew it. He said: Benefit from it, know its length, its parts, and count its number. If its owner comes, Jarir said: No. Save after means: this (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5622","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, that Salamah bin Kuhayl told them, he said: I heard Suwayd bin Ghaflah He says: I, Salman bin Rabi’ah, and Zaid bin Suhan were on a campaign, and I found a whip and took it. When our campaign was completed, I performed Hajj. So I met Ubayy bin Ka’b and asked him about that. He said: “At the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I picked up a bundle containing a hundred dinars. So I brought it to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: He recognized her for a year, so I recognized her, but I did not find anyone who knew her, so I brought her to him, and he said: Identify her. Hula, so I recognized her, but I did not find anyone who knew her, so I went to him. He said: I recognized her as Hula, so I recognized her, but I did not find anyone who knew her, so I went to him. He said: “Memorize its number, its container, and its agents, and enjoy it.” So I enjoyed it.” Amr ibn Yazid told us. He said: Thana. Bahz, he said: Thana Shu’bah, with this chain of transmission and something similar. Shu’bah said: So I heard him ten years later, and he said: “He recognized her for one year.” Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Muhammad told us, Shu’bah told us, with this chain of transmission, and something like it. He said: I met him after that in Mecca, and he said: No. I know three situations or one situation (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5623","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, he said: Suwayd bin told me. He was negligent. He said: I went out with Zaid bin Suhan and Salman bin Rabi’ah, and I picked up a whip with the stick, and they said: Leave it. I said: Don’t let him eat it. The wild beasts, benefit from them, so I brought them to Ubayy ibn Ka’b and told him the hadith, and he said: Well done. “I found it at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then I brought it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: I knew her for a year, so I knew her for a year, then I came to him for the second year, and he said: He recognized her, so I recognized her for one year, then I came to him, and he said: He recognized her, so I recognized her, then I came to him for the third year, and he said Know its number, its vessel, and its agent. If someone comes telling its number, its vessel, and its agent, then give it to him. Otherwise, So benefit from it.”"
"5624","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, then Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he was asked “about the snapshot,” and he said: “Some of it was in the dead road and the common village.” So let it be known for a year, and if its owner comes, give it to him, but if he does not come, then it is yours, and if it is in ruins, then it is in it, and in the five pillars.”"
"5625","Al-Harith bin Miskin, I read about it while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, who said: Amr bin Al-Harith and Hisham bin Saad told me, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that a man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “How about what was found on the dead road? Or in the inhabited town? He said: Identify a Sunnah, and if he comes seeking it, push it to him. Otherwise, it is your business. He said: If he comes He asked for it one day, and it was returned to him, and there was nothing on the road but a dead end, and in an uninhabited town, in it, and in the five pillars.”"
"5626","5668 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Al-Akhnas, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, On the authority of his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about the shoot, and he said: It was not on the road to Matti, or in a populated village. So he defined it as a sunnah, and if its owner comes, otherwise it is a share, and as long as it is not on the way to a coming place, or in a populated village, then it is in it and in the five pillars. “Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari opposed him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5627","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Al-Ansari, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Al-Akhnas, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, On the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Abu Tha’labah, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, “Give me a fatwa regarding the spot.” He said: I did not find it on a dead road, or in a village. It is common, so give it a year, if you do not find its owner.” The hadith was cited as (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5628","On the authority of Mahmoud bin Ghaylan, on the authority of Wakee’, and Qubaysa, both on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Talha bin Musarrif, on the authority of Anas, he said: “The Prophet passed by May God bless him and grant him peace, with a date, and he said: Were it not part of charity, I would have eaten it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5629","Ubayd Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, dictating from his book, he said: My uncle, who is Ya’qub bin Ibrahim bin Saad, told me, He said: Laith, who is Ibn Saad, narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aamir bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “The blind women were wounded by a tyrant, and the well was tyrannical, and the mineral was tyrannical, and in the five ores.” Qutaybah ibn Sa’id disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5630","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salamah, and Ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The blind are mighty, the miner is mighty, the well is mighty, and the five ores are mighty.”"
"5631","Qutaibah bin Sa’id informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Sa’id, and Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “The wound of the blind is mighty, the well is mighty, the mineral is mighty, and the five ores are mighty.”"
"5632","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: I am Mansour, and Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “The well is mighty, and the barren are mighty, and the mine is mighty, and in the five ores”"
"5633","5945 Muhammad bin Salamah informed us, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The blind is mighty, the well is mighty, the miner is mighty, and the five ores are mighty.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5634","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hamza bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “While I was sleeping, a cup was brought to me and I drank from it, then I gave my favor to Omar ibn Al-Khattab.” They said: What did you explain it, O Messenger of God? He said: Knowledge?"
"5635","Nuh ibn Habib narrated, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Muammar narrated, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to narrate, He said: “While I was sleeping, I saw that I had been brought a cup, so I drank from it until I could see the irrigation flowing, then I gave my bounty a lifetime. They said: So what? Did you interpret it, O Messenger of God? He said: “Knowledge.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5636","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah told me, he said: Abu Al-Yaman told us, he said: Shuaib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman: Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever God intends good for, He will make him understand the religion, and I am only the judge.” And God gives.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Yunus disagreed with him. He narrated it, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5637","Suwayd bin Nasr reported, saying: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Ishmael, and Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, saying: Jarir and Waki’ reported, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “There is no envy except in two cases: a man who has done it to him.” “God has given him wealth and has given him the power to destroy it in truth, and a man to whom God has given wisdom, he judges by it and teaches it.”"
"5638","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Jarir reported, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “Do not envy except in two cases: a man to whom God gave the Qur’an and he recites it at any time of the night or at any time of the day, and he says: If only I were given the like of what he was given.” I would have done as this man does, and this is a man to whom God has given knowledge.”"
"5639","Ali bin Hajar reported, on the authority of Ismail, who is Ibn Ja’far, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I said: Oh The Messenger of God, “Who will make people happiest with your intercession on the Day of Resurrection?” Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I thought, O Abu Hurairah, that there would be no Someone more deserving of you than you will ask me about this hadith, given your keenness on the hadith: The happiest of people with my intercession on the Day of Resurrection will be the one who says: No. There is no god but Allah, purely from Himself.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5640","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar told us, he said: Hammad bin Osama told us, he said: Burayd bin Abdullah told me, on the authority of his grandfather, Abu Burdah, on the authority of my father Moses, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, the likeness of the guidance and knowledge with which God has sent me is like a rain that has struck the earth. And there was a group of them that accepted the water, and produced pastures and much grass, and of them there were barren trees that held the water, so God benefited. These people drank from it, grazed and irrigated it, and another group came from it, but they are bottoms that do not hold water and do not grow grass. This is the example of one who understands the religion of God, and what God has sent me with benefits him, and he benefits from it, and he knows and is taught, and the example of one who does not raise his head thereby, And he did not accept the guidance of God with which I was sent.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5641","Ahmad ibn Sulayman reported, he said: 'Ubayd Allah ibn Musa said: Isra'il informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: Ubayy ibn Ka'b narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say:\n\n\The mercy of Allah be upon us and upon Musa. Had he not been hasty and felt shy"," and had a sense of shame before his companion—saying"," 'If I ask you about anything after this"," then do not accompany me'—he would indeed have seen wonders from his companion.\"" He said: \""And the Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him"," when he mentioned any of the Prophets"," would begin by saying: 'The mercy of Allah be upon us and upon my brother Salih; the mercy of Allah be upon us and upon my brother 'Ad.' Then he said: 'Musa"," peace and blessings be upon him"," was one day addressing his people when he said to them: \""There is no one on earth more knowledgeable than me.\"" So Allah revealed to him that there was on earth one more knowledgeable than he"," and the sign of that was that he should provision himself with a salted fish"," and when he lost it"," that would be the place where he would find it.' So he set out with his young companion until they reached the place where they had been commanded. When they arrived at the rock"," Musa"," peace and blessings be upon him"," went in search (of the fish)"," while his companion placed the fish upon the rock. It began to move and made its way into the sea"," entering it through a tunnel. His companion said: 'When the Prophet of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," comes"," I will tell him.' But Satan caused him to forget. So they set out and were afflicted with the fatigue and exhaustion that befalls a traveler"," until Musa had passed beyond the point where he had been commanded to stop. Musa said to his companion: 'Bring us our lunch. We have indeed encountered fatigue from this journey of ours.' His companion said: 'O Prophet of Allah"," do you recall when we took shelter at the rock? I forgot the fish—and nothing made me forget it except Satan—that I should tell you about it. It made its way into the sea in a wondrous manner.' He said: 'That is what we were seeking.' So they retraced their steps"," following their tracks"," until they reached the rock. Musa circled around it and found a figure wrapped in a garment. He greeted him"," and he raised his head and said: 'Who are you?' He said: 'Musa.' He said: 'Which Musa?' He said: 'Musa of the Children of Israel.' He said: 'What do you want?' He said: 'I have been told that you possess knowledge"," and I wished to accompany you.' He said: 'You will never be able to have patience with me.' He said: 'You will find me"," if Allah wills"," patient"," and I will not disobey you in any matter.' He said: 'How can you be patient over that of which you have no knowledge?' He said: 'I have been commanded to do so. You will find me"," if Allah wills"," patient.' He said: 'Then if you follow me"," do not ask me about anything until I mention it to you.' So they set out until"," when they boarded a ship"," he (the companion) went out and stayed behind to make a hole in it. Musa said to him: 'Have you made a hole in it to drown its people? You have indeed brought something terrible.' He said: 'Did I not say that you would never be able to have patience with me?' He said: 'Do not take me to task for what I have forgotten"," and do not burden me with difficulty in my affair.' So they set out until"," when they came upon some boys playing on the shore of the sea"," among whom was a boy who was the most handsome and the cleanest of them all"," he killed him. Musa"," peace and blessings be upon him"," was alarmed at that and said: 'You have killed an innocent soul without it being in retaliation for another soul. You have indeed brought something abominable.' He said: 'Did I not tell you that you would never be able to have patience with me?' Then Musa felt a sense of shame before his companion and said: 'If I ask you about anything after this"," then do not accompany me. You have indeed received an excuse from me.' So they set out until"," when they came to the people of a miserly village"," and Musa was exhausted"," they did not extend hospitality to them. They found in it a wall that was about to collapse"," and he set it upright. Musa said to him"," on account of the exhaustion that had befallen him: 'If you had wished"," you could have taken a wage for it.' He said: 'This is the parting between you and me.' Musa took hold of the edge of his garment and said: 'Tell me (the explanation).' He said: 'As for the ship"," it belonged to poor people who worked on the sea"," and behind them was a king who was seizing every ship by force. When he passed by it and saw it damaged"," he left them alone"," and its people repaired it with a piece of wood and made use of it. As for the boy"," he was"," from the day he was created"," a disbeliever by nature"," and great love had been placed in his parents for him. Had they disobeyed him in anything"," he would have driven them to transgression and disbelief. So we wished that their Lord would give them in exchange one better than him in purity and closer in mercy. Then his father lay with his mother"," and she bore one better than him in purity and closer in mercy. As for the wall"," it belonged to two orphan boys in the city"," and beneath it was a treasure belonging to them"," and their father had been a righteous man. So your Lord intended that they reach their full strength and extract their treasure"," as a mercy from your Lord. And I did not do it of my own accord. That is the interpretation of that over which you could not bear patience.'\"""""
"5642","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, saying: Issa bin Yunus reported, saying: Omar bin Saeed bin Abi Husayn narrated to me, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Uqba. Ibn Al-Harith said: “He married the daughter of Abu Ihab, and a woman from the people of Mecca came on the morning of her reign and said: I have breastfed you both. So she asked the maid’s family, and they denied that, so I rode to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in Medina, so I mentioned that to him. I said: O Messenger of God, I asked the family of the slave girl, and they denied that. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: How, when it was said, how? It was said, “So he separated from her, and she married someone else.”"
"5643","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of Abu Shurayh Al-Adawi, that he said: To Amr bin Saeed He is Ibn Al-Asi, and he is sending an envoy to Mecca: “Permit me, O prince, that I may tell you something that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said.” Tomorrow, from the day of conquest, my ears heard it, my heart understood it, and my eyes saw it when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke about it: Praise be to Him. God, and praised him, then said: God made Mecca sacred, but the people did not make it sacred, and it is not permissible for a person who believes in God and the Last Day to He will not shed blood therein, and he will not uphold a tree therewith. If anyone gives permission to fight the Messenger of God therein, then say, “God has permitted His Messenger, but he has not He gives you permission, but he only granted me an hour during the day, and her sanctity today has resumed as it was yesterday, and let the witness be informed. “The Absent One.” Then it was said to Abu Shuraih: What did Amr tell you? He said: I know that from you, O Abu Shurayh. The Sacred Mosque does not protect a sinner, nor one who flees for blood, nor one who flees with a spear."
"5644","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, saying: Shu’bah narrated to us, he said: Omar bin Sa’id narrated to me. Suleiman, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Aban bin Uthman bin Affan, on the authority of his father, who said: Zayd bin Thabit went out from Marwan, close to Midday, so I went up to him and asked him, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “May God bless a man who heard a conversation from us.” He memorized it until someone else conveyed it to him, for perhaps he is the bearer of jurisprudence to someone who is more knowledgeable than him, and perhaps he is the bearer of jurisprudence who is not a jurist.”"
"5645","Al-Fadl bin Al-Abbas bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Affan told us, he said: Hammam told us, he said: Zaid bin Aslam told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Tell about the Children of Israel and do not be embarrassed, and talk about me and do not lie.” \Ali\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5646","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Muhammad told us, saying: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza: I was translating between Ibn Abbas and the people. Then a woman came to him and asked him about the wine of the draft. He forbade it, saying: The delegation of Abdul Qais came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. They said: O Messenger of God, we are coming to you from a far distance, and there is a lot of harm between us and you, and we cannot come to you. Except in a sacred month, then we were commanded about a matter that we should inform those behind us and thereby enter Paradise. So he commanded them to do four and forbade them from four: He commanded them to believe in God alone, with no partner, and said: Do you know what faith in God is? They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: Bearing witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, establishing prayer, paying zakat, and fasting. Ramadan, and to give one-fifth of the spoils, and he forbade them from beasts of war, and hentam, and earthenware.” Shu’bah said: And perhaps he said: Al-Naqir, Perhaps he said: Al-Muqayyar, so he said: Preserve it, and tell about it to those behind you. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5647","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Amir told us, he said: Qurrah bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, he said: Abdul Rahman told me Ibn Abi Bakra, and a man who in my mind is better than Abd al-Rahman: Humaid bin Abd al-Rahman, both of them on the authority of Abi Bakra, and he said: “We engaged The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the Day of Sacrifice, said: Your blood and your property are sacred among you, just as this day of yours is sacred to you, in your month. This, in this country of yours, until the day you meet your Lord. Have I not conveyed the message? They said: Yes. He said: O God, bear witness. The witness among you will convey the message. The one who is absent, perhaps one who conveys it is more aware than one who hears.” Abridged (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5648","Suleiman bin Salam narrated, he said: Al-Nadr narrated, he said: Ibn Aoun narrated, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakra, on the authority of Abu Bakra, He said: “When that day occurred, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat on his camel and said: What day is this? He said: We remained silent until we thought that it was He will call it something other than its name. He said: Isn’t it the Day of Prohibition? We said: Yes. He said: What month is this? We remained silent until we thought he would name it. He changed his name. He said: Isn’t it Dhul-Hijjah? We said: Yes. He said: What city is this? He said: So we remained silent until we thought that he would call it something else? His name. He said: Isn’t it in the town? So we said: Yes. He said: Your blood, your property and your honor among you are sacred, as is the sacredness of this day of yours. “In this month of yours, in this country of yours, not to inform the absent witness, for perhaps the witness will be informed by someone who is more knowledgeable than him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5649","Zakaria bin Yahya reported, saying: Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq reported, saying: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid. Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and there were men in the house, including Omar bin Al-Khattab, Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Come, I will write for you a letter after which you will never go astray. Then Omar said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He was overcome with pain, and you have the Qur’an. The Book of God is sufficient for us. So they gathered in the house, and some people said: Come near and He will write a letter for you. You will never go astray after him. And some people said: What did Omar say? When the confusion and disagreement increased before the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said To them: Get up. Ubayd Allah said: Ibn Abbas used to say: Pity is all the pity that has not been mentioned from the book that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, intended. And granted that it is written that they will never go astray after him, since their confusion and disagreements have increased.”"
"5650","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Sufyan reported, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ibn Munabbih, on the authority of his brother, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah, saying: “What No one spoke more than me on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, except for Abdullah bin Amr, for he was writing and I was I don't write"
"5651","Muhammad bin Mansour reported, on the authority of Sufyan, who said: I heard Sulayman, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: “On Thursday, and on the On Thursday? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, felt pain intensified, so he said: Bring me that I may write for you a letter after which you will never go astray. Then they quarreled, and do not There must be a dispute with the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. They said: What is the matter with him? Did he leave him? They went to discuss it again. He said: Leave me, for what I am in is better than what you are calling me to. And he advised them upon his death, saying: Expel the polytheists from the Arabian Peninsula. And they treated the delegation in the same way I used to treat them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5652","Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazyd reported, saying: My father told me, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, and Muhammad bin Abdul-Rahman bin Ash’ath reported, saying: Abu Mushar narrated to us, he said: Ismail, who is Ibn Sama’ah, narrated to us, he said: Al-Awza’i narrated to us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir narrated to me, He said: Abu Salamah told me, he said: Abu Hurairah told me, he said: “When Mecca was conquered, Hudhayl killed a man from Bani Laith by killing them. During the pre-Islamic era, this was reported to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he stood up and said: God has withheld the elephant from Mecca, and His Messenger has given it control. And the believers, it was not made lawful for anyone before me, and it will not be made lawful for anyone after me. Rather, it was made lawful for me for an hour of the day, and this is my hour. It is forbidden: its trees are not to be uprooted, its thorns are not to be plucked, and its fallen ones are not to be picked up except seeking one, and whoever is killed for whom someone is killed is of the best of both worlds, either Either he will be led or he will be ransomed. Then a man from the people of Yemen called Abu Shah stood up and said: O Messenger of God, write for me. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Write for Abu Shah. Then Al-Abbas stood up and said: O Messenger of God, except for the Idhkhir, for we put it in our homes and graves. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Except for Al-Idhkhir. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5653","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim reported, on the authority of Uthman bin Omar, who said: Qurrah bin Khalid reported, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “He called for a scroll during his illness to write in it a letter for his nation that they would not go astray after him, nor will they be led astray. And there was a commotion in the house. Then Omar spoke and left him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5654","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak reported, on the authority of Waki’, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Talha bin Musarrif, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “Thursday, and what is Thursday? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Bring me the tablet and the inkwell, or shoulder and inkwell, that I may write for you a book after which you will never go astray.” They said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, will shun.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5655","Abu Dawud reported, he said: Ya’qub told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah told me Abdullah bin Abbas told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “wrote to Caesar inviting him to Islam, and he sent his letter with Dihya al-Kalbi, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to give him to the Azim of Busra so that he could hand him over to Caesar, so the Azim of Busra gave him \to Caesar\"""""
"5656","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Suleiman told us, he said: Ibrahim told us, he said: Saleh bin Kaysan told me, and my nephew Ibn Shihab, both on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent Abdullah bin Hudhafa wrote his letter to Khosrau, giving him the governor of Bahrain, so the governor of Bahrain gave him to Khosrau, and when he read it \His clumsiness\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5657","Humayd ibn Masada reported on the authority of Bishr, who is Ibn al-Mufaddal, who said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted May God bless him and grant him peace, that he should write to the Romans, and they said: They do not read a book unless it is sealed, so he took a silver ring, as if I were looking at it. To the whiteness of it in his hand, and engraved on it: Muhammad is the Messenger of God. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5658","Muhammad ibn Adam reported, on the authority of Abd al-Rahim, who is Ibn Sulaiman, on the authority of Suleiman al-Shaybani, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote to the people of Jerash, forbidding them from mixing dates and raisins. And about dates and dates.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5659","Ahmad ibn Harb reported, saying: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Messenger of God wrote May God bless him and grant him peace to the people of Jerash, forbidding them from mixing dates and raisins."
"5660","5700 Muhammad bin Muammar reported, he said: Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, he said: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: We were forbidden in the Qur’an. To ask the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about something. We were amazed when a sensible man from the desert people would come and ask him, so a man came. From the people of the desert, he said: O Muhammad, your messenger came to us and told us that you claim that God sent you. He said: He spoke the truth. He said: Who created The sky? He said: God. He said: Who created the earth? He said: God. He said: Who placed the mountains on it? He said: Who created therein the benefits? He said: God. He said: By the One who created the heavens and the earth, and set up mountains therein, and created therein benefits, has God sent you? He said: Yes. He said: And he claimed Your Messenger, that upon us are five prayers every day and night. He said: He spoke the truth. He said: By the One who sent you, did God command you to do this? He said: Yes. He said: Your messenger claimed that we owe zakat on our wealth. He said: He spoke the truth. He said: By the One who sent you, did God command you to do this? He said: Yes. He said: And he claimed Your Messenger, that we must fast for a month every year. He said: He spoke the truth. He said: By the One who sent you, did God command you to do this? He said: Yes. He said: And he claimed Your Messenger, that Hajj is upon us, whoever is able to do it. He said: He spoke the truth. He said: By the One who sent you, did God command you to do this? He said: Yes. He said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I will neither add nor subtract from them. When he passed away, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If he is truthful, they will enter Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5661","Muhammad bin Salamah told us, I am Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, Ibn Shihab told me, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas said: “I came riding on a donkey, and that day I was about to have a wet dream, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He was leading the people in Mina, so I passed in front of some of the queue, then I got down and sent the donkey to graze, and I entered the queue, and no one denied it to me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5662","Muhammad bin Al-Musaffa reported, saying: Muhammad bin Harb told us, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Al-Rabi’ Al-Ansari, and he “claimed He met the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when he was five years old, and he claimed that he was wise in a situation that was praised by the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And a ladder from a bucket hanging in their house.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5663","Muhammad bin Khalid reported, saying: Bishr bin Shuaib told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab and Abu Salamah informed me Ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: “You say: Abu Hurairah narrates a lot on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And they say: What is the matter with the Muhajireen and Ansar? They do not find anything like Abu Hurairah on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace The Muhajireen would be occupied with trading in the markets, and my Ansar brothers would be preoccupied with making their money, and I was a poor woman. Poor people of Suffah, I compel the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to fill my stomach, so I am present when they are absent, and I am conscious when they forget, and he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said in a hadith that he narrated one day: No one will spread his garment until I fulfill this statement of mine, then He gathers his garment to him unless he realizes what I am saying, so I spread a sign over me, so that when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made his statement, I gathered it to My heart, I have not forgotten anything about the words of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5664","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim and Ali bin Muhammad bin Ali told me, saying: Ishaq told us, meaning Ibn Isa. He said: Malik told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: “The people say: Abu Hurairah increased it, and by God, if it were not for two verses in the Book of God, I would not have narrated it.” A hadith, then he recites: Indeed, those who conceal the proofs and the guidance We have sent down, after We have made them clear to the people in the Book, to those who repent. Al-Rahim, and he says following the two verses: Our brothers among the Ansar were busy working with their wealth, and our brothers among the Muhajireen were They are occupied with crowding in the markets, and Abu Hurairah used to stay with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to satisfy his stomach, and he would attend what they would not attend. And he memorizes what they do not memorize.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5665","Muhammad bin Mansour reported, saying: Sufyan told us, saying: Al-Zuhri told us, saying: I heard Abd al-Rahman al-Araj saying: I heard Abu Hurairah He says: “You claim that I narrate much on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and God is the Promiser, and that I was a poor person.” I accompanied the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to fill my stomach. The immigrants were busy clapping in the markets, and the Ansar were They are busy taking care of their wealth, so I witnessed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sitting, and he said: Who will spread out his cloak until I make up my mind? My statement, so that he would not forget anything he heard from me. So I spread the cloak that was on me, until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished his statement. Then I added it to me, and by the One who sent him with the truth, I have not forgotten anything I heard from him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5666","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ narrated, on the authority of Abd al-Razzaq, he said: Muammar narrated, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “We used to memorize The hadith, and the hadith is preserved from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but if you ride through every difficulty and humiliation, then that is it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5667","5707 Muhammad bin Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Al-Fadl bin Al-Ala narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Umayyah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qays, on the authority of his father That he told him that a man came to Zayd ibn Thabit and asked him about something, and Zayd said to him: “On you, Abu Hurairah.” “For while I and Abu A kitten and so-and-so in the mosque. One day, when we were praying to God and remembering our Lord, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us and sat down with us. We remained silent, and he said: Go back to where you were. Zaid said: So I and my companion called before Abu Hurairah, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made He greeted us, ensuring our supplication. Then he called Abu Hurairah and said: Oh God, I ask you as these two companions of mine asked you, and I ask you for knowledge. It will not be forgotten. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Amen. He said: O Messenger of God, and we ask God for knowledge that will not be forgotten. He said: He preceded you. “Therein is the young man Al-Dusi.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5668","Nuh bin Habib told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Salem and Abu Bakr bin Sulaiman told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led the evening prayer with us one night at the end of his life, and when he gave the salutation, he said: Have you seen this night of yours? For at the end of a hundred years there will not be a single person left on the surface of the earth."
"5669","Amr bin Mansour reported, he said: Harami bin Hafs told me, he said: Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ulatha told us, he said: Al-Alaa bin Abdullah told me. Al-Hanan bin Kharijah narrated to him on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, who said: While we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, When a man came and said: O Messenger of God, tell us about the garments of Paradise: will they be created? Or will they be woven? Some of the people laughed, He said to them: Are you laughing at an ignorant person asking a scholar? So he sat down for a little while, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Where is the one asking about clothes? Paradise? He said: Here it is, O Messenger of God. He said: No, but the fruits of Paradise will be split from it. He said it three times. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5670","Issa bin Hammad reported, saying: Al-Layth informed us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Sharik bin Abdullah, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He stood up and spoke to the people, then a man stood up and said: “When is the hour, O Messenger of God?” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, smiled at him. So we said to him: Sit down, for you asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, something that he dislikes. Then he got up the second time, and said: O Messenger of God, when? The hour? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked at her more intensely than the first time, then he stood up for the third time and said: O Messenger of God, when is the hour? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Woe to you, and what did you prepare for her? The man said: I prepared for her the love of God and His Messenger, so the Messenger of God said. God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Sit, for you are with whom you love."
"5671","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Jarir reported, on the authority of Abu Farwa, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah bin Amr bin Jarir, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, they said: It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would sit in the presence of his companions, and a stranger would come and not know which one of them he was until he asked. So we asked to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to make a sitting place for him, so that the stranger would recognize him when he came to him. So we built a tent for him out of clay, and it was He would sit on it, and we would sit next to it with two blankets.”"
"5672","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala reported, saying: Khalid, meaning Ibn al-Harith, narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, that Ziyad ibn Ulaqah narrated to them, saying: I heard Usama ibn A partner, who says: “I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and suddenly his companions were with him, and it was as if birds were on their heads.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5673","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Adam told us, he said: Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-Aas, he said: “A group of poor emigrants and I were sitting while sitting beside them. The mosque of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I stood up to them, and he said: Let the poor immigrants give good news of what pleases them, for they are They will enter Paradise forty years before the rich, and I have seen their colors unfold to the point that I wished to be among them.”"
"5674","5714 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak reported, saying: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Ammar bin Ruzaiq told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr Ibn Maimun, on the authority of Muadh Ibn Jabal, said: “I was a companion of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Do you know what God’s right is upon His servants, and what is the right of The servants’ duty to God? I said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: God’s right upon His servants is that they should not associate anything with Him, and the servants’ right upon God is that they should not associate anything with Him. He will punish whoever of them did that.” I said: O Messenger of God, shall I not bring good news to the people? He said: Let them not speak. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5675","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: A man stood up and said: O Messenger of God, “What do you command us to do?” Should we wear clothes in the Sacred Mosque? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not wear shirts, trousers, turbans, or robes. Nor the sandals, unless there is someone who does not have sandals, in which case he should wear socks that are lower than the ankles, and do not wear any clothing that he may touch. “Saffron, nor roses, nor let a woman cover herself forbidden things, nor wear gloves.”"
"5676","5716 Yaqoub bin Ibrahim narrated, saying: Ghandar narrated to us, saying: Muammar narrated to us, saying: Ibn Shihab narrated, on the authority of Issa bin Talha, on the authority of Abd. Allah bin Amr said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, standing on his camel in Mina, and a man came to him and said: O Messenger of God, I used to see that he was shaving before slaughtering, so I shaved before slaughtering. He said: Slay and there is no harm. Then another came to him and said: O Messenger. By God, I used to see slaughter before stoning, so I slaughtered before stoning. He said: So throw it and there is no harm. He said: He was never asked about anything that was presented by a man. Before anything, he said: “Do it, and there is no problem.”"
"5677","Muhammad bin Uthman told us, he said: Bahz bin Asad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Muhammad bin Uthman told us, and his father, Uthman bin Abdullah that they heard Musa bin Talha, narrating on the authority of Abu Ayyub, that a man said: O Messenger of God, “Tell me something that will make me enter Paradise, so the people said: What is his, what is his? So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Arrab, his money? So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him. And peace be upon him: You worship God and do not associate anything with Him, and perform prayer, and pay zakat, and maintain ties with relatives, and leave them as if they were on their mounts.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5678","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, that Ziyad bin Ulaqah told them, he said: I heard Usama bin A partner, he says: “I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and suddenly his companions were with him as if there were birds on their heads.”"
"5679","Muhammad ibn Uthman reported, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Ali ibn Mudarrak, on the authority of Abu Zar’ah, on the authority of Jarir, he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me: “The people listened, and he said: Do not return to being infidels after me, striking the necks of one another.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5680","Abu Dawud narrated, saying: Yazid bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated, on the authority of Al-Rukain bin Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Yahya bin Yamar, and on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa'ib, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, he said: We performed Hajj and Umrah, then we came to Medina, and we came to Ibn Umar and asked him, so we said, O Abu Abd The Most Gracious, we are raiding this land, and we meet a people who say, “There is no destiny.” He turned his face away from us, then said: When you meet those, know. Abdullah bin Omar was innocent of them, so they were innocent of him. Then, he said: “While we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he came A man with a beautiful face, a beautiful appearance, and a pleasant scent. He said: We were impressed by his beautiful face, his appearance, and his pleasant scent. So he greeted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. Then he stood up and said: Shall we approach, O Messenger of God? He said: Yes. He said: We approached. Then he stood up and said: We were amazed at his reverence for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. Then he said: Shall we approach, O Messenger of God? He said: Yes. He said: He approached until he placed his thigh on the thigh of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted another man, then he said: O Messenger of God, what is faith? He said: To believe in God, His angels, His books, and His messengers. And the Last Day, and resurrection after death, and reckoning, and destiny, the good and the bad, the sweet and the bitter. He said: You have spoken the truth. He said: So we were amazed at his saying to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: You have spoken the truth. Then he said: O Messenger of God, what is Islam? He said: You bear witness that there is no god but Him God, and that I am the Messenger of God, and you perform prayer, and pay zakat, and fast Ramadan, and perform Hajj to the House, and wash yourself from ritual impurity. He said: You have spoken the truth. He said: We were amazed at the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, his belief. Then he said: O Messenger of God, what is ihsan? He said: Fear God as if you see Him? If you do not see him, then he sees you. He said: You are right. He said: We were astonished that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, believed him. Then he withdrew and returned. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Ali brings the man, so we looked for him but did not find him. So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: This is Gabriel, he came to teach you about your religion, and he never came to me without me recognizing him, except in this form of his.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5681","Muhammad ibn Al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Bashhar reported on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Qais, who said: I heard Sa’id ibn Amr ibn Saeed bin Al-Asi, that he heard Ibn Omar, speaking on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “We are an illiterate nation, we do not count nor write, the month Thus, thus, and thus, and he held the thumb on the third, and the month is thus, thus, and thus, the completion of the thirty.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5682","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Abu Al-Walid told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mahik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: “We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey.” He said: “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, lagged behind, and we overtook him.” We were exhausted by prayer, so the caller of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called out: “Woe to those who come from the Fire.”"
"5683","Muawiyah bin Saleh reported, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Mubarak, who said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mahak, On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, lagged behind us on a journey we were traveling on, and we found ourselves exhausted by the prayer.” In the afternoon, while we were performing ablution, he made us wipe our feet, then he called out at the top of his voice: “Woe to the hocks from the fire,” two or three times.”"
"5684","Shuaib bin Yusuf reported, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Hisham, who said: My father told me, on the authority of Zainab bint Umm Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that a woman, She said: O Messenger of God, “God is not shy about the truth. Is a woman required to wash herself when she has a wet dream?” He said: Yes, if she sees water. Umm Salamah laughed and said: Does a woman have a wet dream? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What does the boy look like?"
"5685","I am Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala. He said: Khaled told us. He said: Shu’bah told us. He said: Sulayman told me. He said: I heard Mundhir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali, on the authority of Ali, he said: I was ashamed to ask the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, about pre-eclampsia on behalf of Fatima, so I ordered Al-Miqdad and he asked him, He said: In it is ablution. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5686","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, on the authority of, he said: Jarir reported, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to take the time to give us a sermon between days, for fear of boredom upon us.”"
"5687","5727 Muhammad bin Bashar reported, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Abu Al-Tayyah told me, on the authority of Anas, he said: And he said, meaning The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Make things easy and do not make things difficult, give good tidings and do not repel people.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5688","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim reported, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Qais told me, on the authority of Abu Masoud Uqba bin Amr, He said: “A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: ‘I am late for the morning prayer on behalf of so-and-so, which will prolong our stay. I did not see the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he was more angry than he was at a sermon on that day, and he said: O people, some of you are alienated, so which of you has not prayed? “Let him get around people, for among them are the weak, the old, and those in need.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5689","It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said in his sermon: “He praises God and praises Him for what He deserves. Then he says: Who does God guide? So there is no one who can lead him astray, and whoever leads him astray, there is no guide for him. Indeed, the most truthful in speech is the Book of God, and the best of guidance is the guidance of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and evil Matters are newly-invented matters, and every newly-invented matter is an innovation, and every innovation is an error, and every error is in the Fire. Then he will say: I and the Hour will be sent together. Like these two, and whenever the Hour was mentioned, his cheeks would turn red, his voice would rise, and his anger would intensify as if he were the warden of an army, “Good morning, good evening.” Then he said: Whoever leaves behind wealth, it belongs to its owners, and whoever leaves behind debt or loss, it belongs to me and to me, and I am the guardian of the believers. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5690","Abdah bin Abd al-Rahim told me, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Bayan, and Ismail, they said: We heard Qais, saying: I heard Khabbab, He says: “I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was leaning against a cloak in the shade of the Kaaba, and we faced severe distress from the polytheists. So I said: O Messenger of God, will you not pray to God for us? Then he sat down while his face was red and said: Those who came before you should be combed with combs. Iron without its bones, whether flesh or sinew. This does not distract him from his religion. The saw is placed at the joint of his head, and it is cut open. Two do not distract him from his religion, and may God complete this matter until the passenger travels from Sana’a to Hadhramaut fearing no one but God,” a statement added: And the wolf on his sheep"
"5691","Muhammad bin Mansour reported, saying: Sufyan told us, saying: I heard Ayoub, telling about Ata’, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas, saying: I bear witness “I witnessed the Eid with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” So he began to pray before the sermon, then he addressed them, and he saw that he did not He listens to the women, so he came to the women and exhorted them, reminded them, and commanded them to give charity, and with him was Bilal, who said in his dress like this,” meaning: he conquered him. So the woman started throwing the earrings, the ring, and the thing.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5692","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Abd al-Malik bin Abi Suleiman told us, he said: Ata told us, on the authority of Jabir, He said: “I witnessed the prayer with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Eid.” So he began to pray before the sermon, without the call to prayer or iqama. When he finished the prayer, he stood up, leaning on Bilal, and thanked God and praised Him. He preached to the people, reminded them, and urged them to obey him. He went on to The women, with Bilal with him, so he commanded them to fear God, and he advised them and reminded them, and he thanked God and praised Him, then he urged them to obey Him. Then he said: Give charity, for most of you are the firewood of Hell. A woman from the lowliest of people, with pale cheeks, said: For what, O Messenger of God? He said: Because of your many complaints, and your ungratefulness to your spouse, they began to remove their jewelry, their necklaces, their earrings, or their rings, and throw them into the Bilal’s garment, which they give in charity.”"
"5693","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Muhammad told us, saying: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Isbahani, on the authority of Dhakwan, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, that the women said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The men have defeated you, so set a day for us.” We will bring you therein. So he made an appointment with them the next day, and he commanded them and exhorted them, and said: There is no woman among you whose three children die unless they are A shield from the Fire. A woman said: And two? For two have died for me. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And two? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5694","Ahmad bin Sulaiman reported, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, he said: Israel reported, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Saeed, On the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that a woman said to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Give us a day from you.” He said: Such-and-such day. In such-and-such a place, he came to them and taught them the Sunnah, and said: There is no woman who presents three people in front of her without them as a veil for her. From the Fire. A woman said: Or two, O Messenger of God? He remained silent. She said: Or two, O Messenger of God? He said: Or two? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5695","Muhammad bin Mansour reported, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Suhail told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: A woman said: “I do not We were able to let you sit with the men, so he promised us a day on which we would come to you, and he said: Your appointment is at the house of so-and-so, so he came to them, and as he spoke to them, it was: Any woman who has three children die and she is rewarded will enter Paradise. A woman said: Or two? He said: Or two? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5696","Hanad bin Al-Sari reported, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, who said: “When we came to see the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he was sitting “One of us is where it ends.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5697","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, and Al-Harith bin Miskin, a reading of it while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: He reported Malik, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, that Abu Murrah, the client of Aqeel bin Abi Talib, told him on the authority of Abu Waqid Al-Laythi, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “while he was sitting in the mosque and the people were with him, when three people approached. Two went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: And one went, saying: They stopped at the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. One of them saw a gap in the circle and sat in it. As for the other, he sat behind them. As for the third, he turned away and went. When the Messenger of God had finished, May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: Shall I not tell you about the three people? So God was ashamed of him, and as for the other one, he turned away, so God turned away from him.” And in the hadith of Al-Harith: When they stopped at the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, And he delivered a ladder"
"5698","Ali bin Saeed bin Jarir told us, he said: Abd al-Samad told us, he said: Harb bin Shaddad told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us, he said: Ishaq bin told me. Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Abu Murrah, that Abu Waqid Al-Laythi narrated to him, saying: “While we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He greeted him, when three people passed by him, and one of them came and found an opening in a circle and sat down, and the other came and sat behind them, and the third set off. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Shall I not tell you the news of these people? They said: Yes, he said: As for the one who came and sat down: a servant took shelter, so he gave him shelter. God, and as for the one who sat behind you: he was ashamed, so God was ashamed of him, and as for the one who went off: he was a man who turned away, so God turned away from him.”"
"5699","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, he said: Nafi’ told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, that a man stood up in the mosque and said: Oh The Messenger of God, “Where do you order us to perform the Ihram from?” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The people of Medina should perform the Ihram from Dhu al-Hulayfah, and the people of The Levant is from Al-Juhfa, and the people of Najd perform ihram from Qarn.” Ibn Umar said: And they claim that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He performs ihram The people of Yemen are from Yalamlam.” Then Ibn Umar used to say: “I did not learn this from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"5700","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala reported, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, that the Mother of the Believers said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If your people were not modern and had lived in ignorance, I would have demolished the Kaaba and created two gates for it.” When he became king, Ibn Al-Zubayr gave it two doors (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5701","Muhammad ibn Salamah and al-Harith ibn Miskin narrated a reading from him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim. He said: Malik narrated to me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah, that Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abi Bakr Al-Siddiq told Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Aisha, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Did you not see that when your people built the Kaaba, they limited themselves to the foundations of Abraham?” So I said: Oh Messenger of God, will you not return it to the rules of Abraham? He said: “If it had not been for your people’s accusation of disbelief,” Mukhtasar? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5702","Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Tayyah, he said: Anas bin Malik told us, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Among the signs of the Hour are that knowledge will be removed, ignorance will be established, alcohol will be consumed, and adultery will become apparent.”"
"5703","5743 Amr bin Ali and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, saying: Shu’bah told us, saying: I heard Qatada, speaking on the authority of Anas bin Malik, saying: “ Shall I not narrate to you a hadith that I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that no one after me will narrate to you that he heard from him: Indeed, one of the signs of the Hour is that it will be raised. knowledge, ignorance appears, adultery is widespread, alcohol is drunk, the men leave, and the women remain, until there are fifty women. \one curator\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5704","Amr bin Ali reported, saying: Abdul Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told me, saying: Ayoub and Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Asi, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God does not take knowledge by snatching it away.” He snatches it from the scholars, but he seizes the scholar with his knowledge. If there is no scholar left, the people take ignorant people as their heads. They are asked and they give a fatwa. Without knowledge, they went astray and went astray.” Abdul Wahhab said: “I met Hisham bin Urwa, and he told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, the same (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5705","Muhammad bin Rafi’ narrated, saying: Abdul Razzaq narrated to us, saying: Muammar narrated, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God does not take away knowledge from people after He has given it to them, but He takes away the scholars, whenever He went with a scholar who went with what knowledge he had, until those who did not know remained, and they went astray and were misled.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5706","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman reported, saying: Abdullah bin Wahb told us, saying: I heard Al-Layth bin Saad, saying: Ibrahim bin Abi Abla told me, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Jurashi, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, said: Awf bin Malik Al-Ashja’i told me that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him “One day he looked at the sky and said: This is the time for the flag to be raised,” and a man from the Ansar called Labid bin Ziyad said: O Messenger of God. Is knowledge being raised while hearts have attained it? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “If I were to consider you among the most knowledgeable of people.” Medina, and he mentioned to him the misguidance of the Jews and Christians based on the Book of God in their hands. He said: I met Shaddad bin Aws, and I spoke to him. According to the hadith of Awf bin Malik, he said: Awf spoke the truth. Shall I not tell you the first thing that will be raised? I said: Yes, he said: Humility, so that you will not see someone humble?"
"5707","Muhammad bin Muammar told us, he said: Muhammad bin Abbad Al-Hinai told us, he said: Ali bin Al-Mubarak Al-Hinai told us, he said: Ayoub Al-Sakhtiyaani told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Al-Duraik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever learns knowledge for other than God, or wants other than God, so let him take his seat in the Fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5708","Ismail bin Masoud narrated, saying: Khalid narrated, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, and Muhammad bin Bashar narrated, saying: Yahya narrated, on the authority of Shu’bah, He said: Mansour told me, he said: I heard a quarter, saying: I heard Ali, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not lie to me. For whoever lies about me will enter Hell.” And Muhammad said: “Whoever lies about me (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5709","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala informed me, he said: Khalid told us, on the authority of Shu`bah, he said: Jami` ibn Shaddad informed me, he said: I heard Aamir ibn Abdullah ibn Al-Zubair, narrating on the authority of his father, that he said to Al-Zubair: “Why do I not see you narrating anything on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: I did not leave him. Since I converted to Islam, but I heard him say: Whoever lies to me, let him take his seat in the Fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5710","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdul Aziz told us, and Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us. He said: Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever deliberately tells a lie against me, Let him take his seat in the Fire.” Abdul-Warith said in his hadith: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying"
"5711","Ali bin Hajar reported, he said: Ismail reported, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, he said: Anas bin Malik told us, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who He lied about me, so let him take his seat in the Fire, intentionally.” He said: Anas reported like this twice, then he would command him again. He said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever lies about me intentionally, let him take his seat in Hell.”"
"5712","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan reported, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu`bah told me, he said: Abu Husayn told me, he said: I heard Abu Saleh, on the authority of my father Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever lies about me intentionally, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"
"5713","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Amr bin Aws, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr Ibn Al-Aas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, those who are just in the sight of God Almighty will be on platforms of light at the right hand of the Most Gracious, those who do justice.” concerning their rule, their families, and what they were given over to them.” Muhammad said in his hadith: And both of his hands were on the right. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5714","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, those who are just in God will be on platforms of light on the Day of Resurrection in the hands of the Most Gracious, as “Be just in this world.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Shuaib bin Abi Hamza made him stop. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5715","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad, he said: Yazid bin Abdullah bin Usama bin Al-Had told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Busr bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Qais, the client of Amr bin Al-Asi, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Aas, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “If a judge rules and tries hard and is correct, he will have two rewards, and if he rules and tries hard and is wrong, he will have one reward.” Ibn al-Haad said: I told Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Hazm, and he said: This is how Abu Salamah told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. Ishaq said: : I did not understand Amr ibn al-Aas from Abdul Aziz. Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am the reciter. He said: Haywa bin Shurayh narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Had, both hadiths. With their chain of transmission the same, like it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5716","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Hazm, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If the ruler rules, “So he worked hard and got it right, he will have two rewards, and if he worked hard and made a mistake, he has a reward.”"
"5717","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Khubayb bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Hafs bin Asim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There are seven whom God will shade on the Day of Resurrection with His shade, a day when there will be no shade but His shade: an imam A just man, a young man who grew up worshiping God Almighty, a man who mentioned God in private and his eyes filled with tears, and a man whose heart was attached to the mosque. And two men loved each other for the sake of God Almighty, and a man was invited by a woman of position and beauty to herself, and he said: I fear God Almighty. And a man gave charity and hid it so that his left hand would not know what his right hand had done.”"
"5718","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Saeed bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, he said: Abu Hashim told us, he said: If it were not for the hadith of Ibn Buraydah On the authority of his father, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I would have said: “If the judge tries hard, there is nothing on him, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: There are three judges, two in Hell and one in Paradise: a man who knew the truth and decided according to it, then he will be in Paradise, and a man who knew “And a man who did not know the truth, so he ruled for the people out of ignorance, will be in Hell.”"
"5719","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya al-Baghdadi informed us that he was known to have been struck by a lightning bolt. He said: Mu’alla ibn Mansour told me, Dawud ibn Khalid told us, he heard Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever is appointed a judge has been slaughtered without a knife.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5720","Abu Dawud Suleiman bin Saif Al-Harrani told us, Abu Ali, the Hanafi, told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, Othman bin Muhammad told me Al-Akhnasi, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is appointed to judge, It is as if he had been slaughtered with a knife.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Othman bin Muhammad al-Akhnasi is not that strong man. We only mentioned him so that he would not go out. Othman is from the middle, and he says: Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Saeed (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5721","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Safwan bin Issa told us, he said: Abdullah bin Saeed bin Abi Hind told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Othman, he said: Abu Abdul Rahman, and the correct one is Othman bin Muhammad, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And he said: “Whoever is appointed a judge will be slaughtered without a knife.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5722","Muhammad bin Abdul Rahim told us, he said: I am Abu Salamah Al-Khuza’i Mansour bin Salamah, he said: Abdullah bin Ja’far, he is Al-Makhrami, told us. On the authority of Uthman ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever is appointed a judge among the people will be slaughtered.” Without a knife.” Abu Salamah said: He mentioned it once or twice, on the authority of Al-Araj and Al-Maqbari. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5723","5762 Muhammad ibn Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn al-Mubarak, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “You will strive for the emirate, but it will be a matter of regret and regret on the Day of Resurrection, so blessed is the wet nurse. “Wretched is Fatima.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5724","Yazid bin Sinan told us, he said: Abdullah bin Hamran told us, Abdul Hamid said, Saeed bin Abi Saeed Al-Maqbari told us, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Hakam On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he used to say: “You will be keen on the emirate, but it will be a regret and a regret on the Day of Resurrection.” So the suckling woman was blessed, but miserable was the Fatima woman.”"
"5725","Mujahid bin Musa told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Samurah, and Amr told us Ibn Ali, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “Do not ask for leadership, for if you give it to her for a question to which you have been entrusted, and if you give it to her for another question, you will be assisted.” \on her\"""""
"5726","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of his brother, on the authority of Abu Burdah, On the authority of Abu Musa, he said: “Two men from the Ash’aris came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they began to propose work, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Indeed, the most trustworthy of you in my eyes is the one who seeks him, but does not seek their help for anything.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abbad ibn al-Awwam entered between His brother and Abu Burdah, Qurrah bin Bishr. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5727","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub and Hilal bin Al-Ala told me, and the word for it, they said: Saeed bin Suleiman told us, he said: Abbad bin Al-Awam told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of his brother, on the authority of Qurrah bin Bishr, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Me and two men, and one of them testified and said: O Messenger of God, we have come for you to seek help from us in some of your work, and the other testified, so he said Like the first article, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, your brother is the one who is the most betrayed to me, and he is seeking him.” He did not seek help from them in anything until he was arrested."
"5728","5955 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Qurrah bin Khalid told us, he said: Humaid bin Hilal told us, he said: Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: “I approached the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and with me were two men from the Ash’arites, one of them to my right, and the other to my right.” Yasari and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, were silent. They both asked about work. I said: By the One who sent you with the truth, they did not inform me of what was in it. themselves, and I did not feel that they were asking for work. It was as if I was looking at his toothbrush. Under his lip it had contracted. He said: I do not or I will not. We will assign whomever he wants to do our work, but you go. He sent him to Yemen, then Muadh bin Jabal followed him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5729","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I heard Anas, speaking on the authority of Usayd Ibn Hudayr, that a man from the Ansar came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “Are you not going to use me as you used so-and-so?” He said: “You are After me you will meet a trail, so be patient until you meet me at the basin.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5730","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Samurah, he said: He said, meaning the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Do not ask for leadership, for if you give it to it for a question, it is entrusted to it, and if you give it to it for another question, you will help.” \on her\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5731","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Sulayman bin Harb told us, he said: Omar bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abi Umays, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Burdah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: Some people from the Ash’arites came to me and said: Go with us to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. We have a need, so I went with them, and they said: O Messenger of God, seek help from us in your work, Abu Musa said, so I apologized for what they said. I was told that I did not know what their need was, so he believed me and excused me, and said: We do not seek help in our work from those who ask us.”"
"5732","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Zaafrani told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Abi Mulaika informed me, that Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr told him that: “The caravan of Banu Tamim came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Abu Bakr said: He commanded Al-Qaqa’ bin Ma’bad, and he said Omar, may God be pleased with him: Rather, he commanded Al-Aqra’ ibn Habis, and they competed until their voices rose, and at that it was revealed: O you who have believed, do not “They advanced before God and His Messenger until the verse was completed. And if they had been patient until it came out to them, it would have been better for them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5733","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Humaid told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, he said: He protected me. By God, with something I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when Khosrau died. He said: “Who did they succeed in? He said: His daughter. He said: He will not succeed.” A people who have appointed a woman as their leader.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5734","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, he said: I heard Abu Umamah, narrating on the authority of Abu Sa`id, that he heard him say: When the people of Qurayza came to the rule of Sa`d, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came on a donkey, and he said: These They submitted to your ruling. He said: “Then I rule that those who fight them should be killed and their descendants taken captive.” He said: “You have ruled over them with the ruling of a king.” Abu Abdul Rahman: Muhammad bin Salih disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5735","5773 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak informed us, he said: Abu Amer told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salih, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Amer bin Saad, on the authority of his father, said that Saad, “He ruled against the Banu Qurayzah that everyone of them who was touched by the razor should be killed, and that she should be taken captive.” Their descendants, and to divide their wealth. This was mentioned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: You have judged them according to the judgment of God who has judged. Therein is above seven heavens.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5736","Qutaibah told us, he said: Yazid told us, meaning bin Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh bin Hani, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his father Shurayh, on the authority of his father Hani’, that: “When he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with his people, he heard them being happy, Abu Al-Hakam, so he called him The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said to him: Indeed, God is the judge, and to Him is the judgement, so why are you given the nickname Abul-Hakam? He said: My people then They disagreed about something. They came to me, so I judged between them, and both parties agreed. He said: What is better than this, so what child do you have? He said: I have a partner. And Abdullah and Muslim, he said: Who is the eldest of them? He said: Shurayh. He said: You are Abu Shurayh, and he prayed for him and his son."
"5737","Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa informed us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Saeed, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “There were kings after Jesus, son of Mary, may God bless him and grant him peace, who changed the Torah and the Gospel, and among them there was Believers read the Torah, and it was said to their kings: We do not find a curse worse than the curse they curse us. They recite: And who does not He judges by what God has sent down. Those are the disbelievers, and these are the verses with which they fault us in our deeds in reciting them, so call upon them. Let them read as we read, and believe as we have believed. So he called them and gathered them together, and proposed that they be killed or they should abandon reading the Torah and the Gospel. Except what they changed, so they said: What do you want to do that? Let us. Then a group of them said: Build a cylinder for us, then raise us to it. Then they gave us something with which to take our food and drink, so that we would not respond to you. A group of them said: Let us roam the land and wander and drink. Just as a wild animal drinks. If you attack us in your land, kill us. A group of them said: Build us a house in the wilderness, and we will celebrate. Wells and we cultivate crops, but we will not respond to you nor pass by you, and there is not one of the tribes except that he has intimate relations with them. He said: So they did that, so it was revealed God Almighty: And monasticism which they invented, We did not prescribe it for them except to seek the pleasure of God, but they did not care for it as it should be cared for. And the others said: We worship as so-and-so worshiped, and we walk as so-and-so wandered, and we adopt a role as so-and-so took, and they are in their polytheism, having no knowledge of the faith of those who They followed his example. When God sent the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and only a few of them remained, a man descended from his cell, and a tourist came from His travel, and the owner of the monastery from his monastery, so they believed in him and believed in him, so God, Blessed and Most High, said: O you who have believed, fear God and believe. By His Messenger, He will give you two parts of His mercy, in reward for their faith in Jesus, peace be upon him, and in the Torah and the Gospel, and their faith in Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace and blessings of God be upon him, and to believe them. He said: And He will make for you a light by which you follow the Qur’an and for them to follow the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: lest The People of the Book who imitate you know that they are not capable of anything of God’s grace, and that grace is in the hand of God. He gives it to whom He wills. And God is the Possessor of great bounty.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5738","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: On the authority of Ali Abi Al-Assad, he said: Bukayr bin Wahb Al-Jazari told us, he said: Anas said. Ibn Malik: “I will tell you a story that I do not tell everyone: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood at a gate while we were there, and he said: The Imams are among Quraysh, they have a right over you, and you have a right over them. If they ask for mercy, they will be granted mercy, and if they make a covenant, they fulfill it, and if they rule, they are just. So whoever does not “Whoever of them does that, the curse of God, the angels, and all of mankind is upon him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5739","Muhammad bin Salamah informed us, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Zainab bint Abi Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I am only human, and you dispute before me, and perhaps some of you will be merciful.” With some evidence from him, then I will pay for him according to what I hear from him. Whoever for whom I decide something that is due to his brother should not take anything from him. “I will only give him a portion of the Fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5740","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abu Amer told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, that He wrote to Omar asking him, so he wrote to him: “I decide according to what is in the Book of God, and if it is not in the Book of God, then according to the Sunnah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” And peace be upon him. If it is not in the Book of God, nor in the Sunnah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then judge according to what the righteous have decreed. The Book of God, nor in the Sunnah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the righteous did not decree it, so if you wish, then move forward, and if you wish, then move back, and do not I think that delay is only good for you, and peace be upon you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5741","Mujahid bin Musa told us, on the authority of Hushaym, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, that A man asked the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “My father’s Hajj has overtaken him, and he is an old man and cannot stand firmly on his camel. If I force him, I fear that he will die.” Should I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: Have you seen that if he had a debt and I paid it off, would it be sufficient? He said: Yes. He said: So perform Hajj on behalf of your father? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5742","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Ishaq told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I was The companion of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a man came to him and said: “My father is old and has not performed Hajj, and if I carried him on a camel he would not stand on him. I forced him to do so. He did not trust him. He said: Would you have settled the debt if he had owed it? He said: Yes. He said: He performed Hajj on behalf of your father. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Muhammad bin Sirin disagreed with him, and said: On the authority of Al-Fadl bin Abbas (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5743","Ahmad bin Sulayman told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Sulayman Ibn Yasar, on the authority of Al-Fadl Ibn Al-Abbas, that he was a companion of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a man came to him and said: O Messenger of God, “My mother An old woman. If I carried her, she would not hold on, and if I tied her up, I feared that I would kill her. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Have you seen? If your mother had a debt, would you have paid it? He said: Yes. He said: Then perform Hajj on behalf of your mother. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5744","Muhammad bin Hashim Al-Baalbaki told us, Al-Walid told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, On the authority of Al-Fadl ibn Al-Abbas, he was the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the morning of the sacrifice, and a woman from Khath’am came to them and said: O Messenger of God, “God’s obligation of Hajj on His servants has caused my father to become an old man, and he cannot ride unless he objects. Should I perform Hajj?” On his behalf? He said: Yes, perform Hajj on his behalf. He said: If he was in debt, did you pay it off? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5745","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Salih bin Kaysan, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Suleiman bin Yassar told him that Ibn Abbas told him that a woman from Khath’am “consulted the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about The Farewell Pilgrimage, and Al-Fadl bin Abbas was the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: O Messenger of God, “It is the obligation of God Almighty to Performing Hajj on behalf of His servants. I met my father as an old man, not equal to a camel woman. Will it suffice for me to perform Hajj on his behalf? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: Yes, so Al-Fadl bin Abbas began to look at her, and she was a beautiful woman, and he took The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned his face to the other side.”"
"5746","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Al-Walid bin Nafi’ told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Ishaq, he said: I heard Suleiman Ibn Yassar, narrating to him on the authority of Al-Fadl Ibn Al-Abbas, he said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Prophet of God, “My father is an old man.” He is old and unable to perform Hajj, and if I carry him and he does not hold back, should I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: Perform Hajj on behalf of your father. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Sulayman did not? He hears from Fadl ibn Abbas (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5747","Muhammad bin Muammar told us, he said: Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Zakaria bin Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’atha’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “My father is an old man, should I perform Hajj on his behalf?” He said: Yes, see if I He owed a debt and I paid it off. Will it be repaid? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5748","Amr bin Uthman told me, he said: Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Ibn Shihab told me, and Mahmoud bin Khalid told me, He said: Omar told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, that Ibn Abbas informed him that a woman from Khath’am “ She consulted the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and virtue is synonymous with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: O Messenger of God, “It is an obligation God Almighty is in the Hajj for His servants. I found that my father was an old man, and he was unable to stand upright on a mount. Would that be sufficient? Mahmoud said: Would he? Should I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said to her: Yes. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This hadith was narrated by more than one person on the authority of al-Zuhri, but he did not mention in it what al-Walid mentioned. Ibn Muslim"
"5749","Al-Harith bin Miskin said, reading it while I was listening, that Ibn al-Qasim, Malik told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Suleiman bin Left, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, who said: “Al-Fadl bin Abbas was the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a woman from Khath'am was asking him for a question, so Al-Fadl looked at her, and she looked at him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned Al-Fadl's face to The other part, and she said: O Messenger of God, “It is the obligation of God Almighty for His servants to perform Hajj. My father became very old and could not perform it.” He stays on the one who is moving, should I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: Yes, and that was during the Farewell Pilgrimage."
"5750","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya al-Qattan told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, he said: my father told me, on the authority of Zainab The daughter of Abi Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You are disputing against me, but I am only a human being, and perhaps Some of you may be more eloquent in your argument than others, so whoever for whom I have decreed something of his brother’s right should not take it, for I will only give him a piece of it for him. \fire\"""""
"5751","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Raqqashi told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, he said: Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Bashir ibn Nahik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Two women disputed with Suleiman ibn Dawud. Peace be upon them, there was a child, each one of them claimed that she had given birth to him. Then the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Bring the knife so we can cut it off. Between them, one of them said: Rather, leave it to her. He said: And the other was satisfied. He said: If he were your son, she would not have consented to him being cut off. So he decided. with it for the Hereafter.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5752","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, he said: Shuaib bin Al-Layth told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, on the authority of Al-Araj, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Two women went out with two of their boys, so the wolf ran over One of them, and he took her child, and they began to dispute over the remaining boy. They disputed with David the Prophet, peace be upon him, and he decided that he should be the eldest. So they passed to Suleiman, peace be upon him, and he said: How did you do? So they told the story to him, and he said: Bring me the knife and I will cut the boy between them. She said: The youngest: Do you tear it apart? He said: Yes, and she said: Do not, give him a share of it for her. He said: It is your son, so he decided for it for her. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5753","Al-Mughirah bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Miskin bin Bukayr Harrani told us, he said: Shuaib bin Abi Hamza told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Two women went out with their children, and the wolf took One of them, so they disputed about the child to David the Prophet, peace be upon him, and he decided for the eldest of them, so they went to Solomon, peace be upon him, and he said: How? It was decided between you? He said: It was decided for the eldest. Solomon said: Cut it in two halves, for this woman half and for the other half. So the eldest woman said: Yes. Cut him off, and the youngest said: Do not cut him off, he is her child. So the ruling was made for the woman who refused to cut him off.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5754","Imran bin Bakkar al-Homsi told us, he said: Ali bin Ayyash al-Homsi told us, he said: Shuaib told us, he said: Abu al-Zinad told me, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj narrated to him, from what he mentioned that he heard Abu Hurairah narrate to him on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: And he said: “While two women had their sons with them, the wolf came and took away the son of one of them, and this woman said to her friend: He only took your son.” And the other said: He only took your son, so they took judgment before David, peace be upon him, and he ruled for him to be the eldest, so they went out to Suleiman bin David. Peace be upon them both. So you told him, and he said: Bring me a knife and I will cut it between them. The younger one said: Do not do that, may God have mercy on you. He is her son. So he ruled for the minor. Abu Hurairah said: By God, I had never heard of a knife except that day. We used to say nothing but a knife."
"5755","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Yahya bin Ma’in told us, he said: Hisham bin Yusuf and Abd al-Razzaq told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Umar, said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent Khalid ibn al-Walid to Bani Jadhimah, and he invited them to Islam.” But they did not do well to say, “We surrender,” so they began to say, “We became youthful,” and he made Khalid among them, killing and capturing them. He said, “And he was pushed to Every man was a captive, until one day, Khalid ibn al-Walid ordered that every man of us kill his own prisoner. Ibn Umar said: So I said: By God, no. I will kill my prisoner and none of my companions will kill his prisoner. He said: So we came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the good deed of Khalid was mentioned to him. He said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, raised his hands: Oh God, I disavow before you what Khaled did.” Zakaria said in his hadith: So he mentioned, and in Bishr’s hadith, He said: “Oh God, I disavow before you what Khaled did.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5756","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: I am Hushaym, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakra, on the authority of his father, he said The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A judge does not decide between two people while he is angry.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5757","Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala and al-Harith ibn Miskin told us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, who said: I read to him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Ibn Yazid, and Al-Layth Ibn Saad, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Urwa Ibn Al-Zubayr narrated to him, that Abdullah Ibn Al-Zubayr narrated to him, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam, “He quarreled with a man from the Ansar who had witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the anus of a free woman. They both watered the palm trees with it, and Al-Ansari said: Let the water pass over it, but he refused to do so, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Water, oh Zubayr, then send water to your neighbor. Al-Ansari got angry and said: O Messenger of God, if he is your cousin? Then the face of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, colored, and then he said: O Zubayr, water, then hold back the water until it returns to the walls, and he took up the water. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave Al-Zubayr his right, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had previously advised Al-Zubayr of an opinion he intended. There is room for him and for the Ansari, so when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, protected the Ansari, he granted al-Zubayr his right to express judgment, he said. Al-Zubair: I do not think this verse was revealed except in this regard: But no, by your Lord, they will not believe until they make you judge in what is disputed between them. And one of them adds more than His companion in the story, Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Qutaybah ibn Sa`id disagreed with him."
"5758","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, that Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr told him that a man from The Ansar disputed with Al-Zubayr to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the annex of Al-Harrah with which they irrigate the palm trees. He said to the Ansari: Let the water pass. He refused, so they disputed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Zubair: “Give water, O Zubair. Then send to your neighbor. The Ansari got angry and said: O Messenger of God, if he was your cousin, then the face of the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became discolored? He greeted him, then said: O Zubair, water it, then withhold the water until it returns to the walls. Al-Zubair said: By God, I think this is the verse. It was revealed about that: “But no, by your Lord, they will not believe until they make you judge in what is a dispute between them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5759","Abu Dawud Suleiman bin Saif told us, he said: Othman bin Omar told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ka’b, on the authority of his father, that: “Ibn Abi Hadrad paid for a debt he owed in the mosque, and their voices rose until the Messenger of God heard them.” While he was in his house, may God bless him and grant him peace, he went out to them and uncovered the curtain of his room. He called out: O Ka’b, and said: At your service, O Messenger. God, he said: Give up this part of your debt, and he gestured to the half, he said: I have done it, he said: Arise and pay it off.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: He sent him Muammar, Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, that Ka’b bin Malik, was sent. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5760","5965 Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abdul-Hakam informed us, on the authority of Shuaib, he said: Al-Layth informed us, on the authority of Ibn al-Had, on the authority of al-Walid ibn Ubayy. Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan Al-Basri, on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You will not believe until you love one another. Shall I not inform you of what you love each other over? They said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: Spread peace among yourselves, for by the One in whose hand is my soul, you will not enter Paradise. Until they showed mercy to each other, they said: O Messenger of God, we are all merciful. He said: It is not the mercy of one of you that belongs to his elite, but the mercy of the common people. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5761","5966 Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Harith Al-Makhzoumi informed us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Sulayman bin Musa said, Nafi’ told us, and Ibn Muhammad told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Sulayman bin Musa told me, on the authority of Nafi’, On the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Spread greetings, spread food, and be brothers as God has commanded you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5762","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Abu Hazim told us, he said: I heard Sahl bin Saad, saying: “It fell between... There was some talk from the Ansar, until they threw stones at each other, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to make peace between them, and the time for prayer came. So Bilal gave the call to prayer, and waited for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he withdrew himself and established the prayer, and Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, came forward and led the people. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and Abu Bakr was leading the people in prayer. When the people saw him, they forgave him, and Abu Bakr did not turn around during prayer, so when he heard Their greeting turned around, and it was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who wanted to be late, so he indicated to him to stand still, so Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, meaning: his hands. Then he recanted, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went forward and prayed. When the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, finished. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: What prevented you from being steadfast? He said: God would not have seen Ibn Abi Quhafa in the hands of His Prophet, then come to the people. He said: What is the matter with you that if something bothers you in your prayer, you forgive? That is for women. If something bothers you in your prayer, let him say: Glory be to God. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5763","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and Zaid bin Khaled, who is Al-Juhani, and Shibl. They said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a man came up to him and said: “I adjure you by God, You have not decided between us according to the Book of God. Then his opponent stood up and was more knowledgeable than him, and said: He has spoken the truth, judge between us according to the Book of God. He said: Say, he said: Indeed, my son He was stubborn about this, so we committed adultery with his wife, so I ransomed him with a hundred sheep and a servant, as if he had been informed that his son would be stoned, so I ransomed him. From him, then I asked men of knowledge, and they told me that my son must be subjected to one hundred lashes and a year of exile, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: And he said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, I will judge between you according to the Book of God: a hundred sheep and a male servant shall be given back to you, and a hundred lashes shall be given to your son. “And a general sojourn, O Unays, go tomorrow against this woman, and if she confesses, stone her.” Then he went to her in the morning and she confessed, so he stoned her. “Abu Abdul Rahman: We do not know of anyone who followed Sufyan on what he said: and a cub. It was narrated by Malik, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and Zayd ibn Khalid, and it was narrated by Bukayr ibn Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Amr ibn Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah only. The hadith of Malik and Amr bin Shuaib is more correct than the statement of Ibn Uyaynah: and Shibl. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5764","5976 Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: I heard Malik bin Anas, and Yunus bin Yazid told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab told him, and Al-Harith bin Maskin, a reading to him while I was hearing, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Yunus and others told me, On the authority of Ibn Shihab, he informed him, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Zayd ibn Khalid, that two men came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He handed over two disputers to him, and one of them said: “Judge between us according to the Book of God.” And the other, who was the more understanding of them, said: Yes, so judge between us according to the Book of God. He gave me permission to speak. He said: Speak. He said: My son was stubborn about this, and that he had committed adultery with his wife. He told me that Ali My son was stoned, so I ransomed him with a hundred sheep and a female slave. Then I asked the people of knowledge, and they told me that my son had to suffer a hundred lashes. And a general exile, but the stoning is for his wife. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, I will decide between you according to a book. By God, as for your flocks and your maidservants, he was restored to you, and he flogged his son for a hundred and exiled him for a year, and commanded Anis to stone the other’s wife if she confessed. So she confessed, so he stoned her.”"
"5765","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, he said: Shuaib bin Al-Layth told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ja’far bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, On the authority of Abdullah bin Ka’b bin Malik Al-Ansari, on the authority of Ka’b bin Malik, “He had a right over Abdullah bin Abi Hadrad Al-Aslami He met him and joined him, and they talked until their voices rose. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by them and said: O Ka’b, so he pointed. With his hand, as if he was saying, “Half,” so he took half of what he owed, and left half."
"5766","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya told us, meaning Ibn Saeed, on the authority of Awf bin Abi Jamila, he said: Hamza Abu Omar told me Al-A’idhi said: Alqamah bin Wa’il told us, on the authority of Wa’il, who said: “I witnessed the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when he brought the killer, led by a guardian. The murdered man was in Nas'ah. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to the guardian of the murdered man: Will you pardon him? He said: No. He said: Do you take the blood money? He said: No. He said: So you kill him. He said: Yes. He said: Go. When he left, he called him and said: Will you pardon? He said: No. He said: Will you take the blood money? He said: No. He said: So you kill him? He said: Yes. He said: Take him away. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If you pardon He committed his own sin and the sin of your companion, so they pardoned him and left him, so I saw him carrying his burden.” Muhammad ibn Bashar told us, He said: Yahya narrated to us. He said: Jami’ bin Matar al-Hatami narrated to us, on the authority of Alqamah bin Wa’il, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, like him. Yahya said: This is better than it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5767","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, that he told him, that Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, He told him that a man from the Ansar “disputed Al-Zubayr to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, over the annulment of Al-Harrah, with which they watered the palm trees.” He said: Al-Ansari: He made the water flow by, but it refused to them, so they disputed with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: To Al-Zubair: Water, O Zubair, then send the water to your neighbour. The Ansari got angry and said: O Messenger of God, if he is your cousin, then he is colourful The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, faced his face, then said: O Zubair, water, then hold back the water until it returns to the walls. Then Al-Zubair said: By God. Indeed, I think that this verse was revealed about that, but no, by your Lord, they do not believe.”"
"5768","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Wahhab told us, he said: Khalid told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the husband of Barira was a slave called: Mughith, as if I could see him walking around behind her, crying, with his tears running down his beard, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him, to Abbas: O Abbas, are you not amazed at Mughith’s love for Barira, and at Barira’s hatred of Mughith? Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: If you go back to him, he is the father of your child. She said: O Messenger of God, do you command me? He said: I am only an intercessor. She said: I have no need of him. Abu Abdul Rahman: This is a valid hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5769","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Thana Al-Mughirah, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Abd al-Majid bin Suhail, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, “A man from the Ansar freed a slave of his who was in need, and he mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He, peace and blessings be upon him, called him and said: Have you freed your servant? He said: Yes, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You are more in need of it, then he said: Who will buy it? Nuaym bin Abdullah said: “I am.” So he bought it, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took its price and gave it to its owner. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5770","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Al-Ala told us, on the authority of Ma’abad bin Ka’b, on the authority of his brother Abdullah bin Ka’b, On the authority of Abu Umamah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever takes away the rights of a Muslim man by taking an oath, God has made Hell fire necessary for him. And Paradise was forbidden to him, and a man said to him: Even if it is a small thing, O Messenger of God. He said: Even if it is a short period of time?"
"5771","Harun bin Abdullah told us, he said: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b, that he heard his brother Abd Allah bin Ka’b narrated that Abu Umamah Al-Harithi narrated to him that he heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “No man takes away a man’s rights.” With his right hand, God has forbidden him Paradise and required Hell for him. Then a man from among the people said: O Messenger of God, even if it is a small thing? He said: Even if it is a siwak from Arak. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5772","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, She said: Hind bint Utbah came and said: “My husband, Abu Sufyan, is a stingy, stingy man. He does not give me enough for me and my children. Should I take from What is his money when he does not know? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Take what is sufficient for you and your children, on a fair basis."
"5773","Al-Hussein bin Mansour bin Jafar Al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Mubashir bin Abdullah Al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Sufyan bin Husayn, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Iyas, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakra, who was a worker at Sijistan, who said: Abu Bakra wrote to me, He says: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “No one makes a decision in a matter with two decisions, and no one makes a decision between two adversaries while he is \angry\"""""
"5774","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abdul Razzaq, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Zainab bint Abi Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, heard an opponent’s meal at Umm Salamah’s door, so he went out to them and said: “You are quarreling.” To me, but I am only a human being, and perhaps some of you are more knowledgeable about his argument than others, so I will judge for him according to what I hear, and I think he is telling the truth. “For whomever I have fulfilled the rights of his brother, it is only a piece of Hell, let him take it or leave it.”"
"5775","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Waki` told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Zainab bint Umm Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You are disputing against me, but I am only human, and perhaps some of you have composed an argument with me.” From each other, I will only judge between you according to what I hear. So whoever for whom I have fulfilled anything that is due to his brother, I will only grant him a portion of the Fire.”"
